  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Change Advocacy in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate change poses immense challenges to the lives and livelihoods of many people in Kenya. For instance through recurrent droughts, drying of water sources, erratic rainfall, flash floods and landslides and the spread of diseases like Malaria. 
Therefore this project aims to create a people free from the vulnerabilities of climate change, and empowered by the improvements to their livelihoods. 

The project seeks to achieve this through 4 closely interlinked outcomes which include; a positive policy and legislative framework being in place, strengthened participation of Kenyans in the climate change debates at the local, national and international level; vulnerability of poor communities to climate change in Kenya being reduced.

The proposed project will be implemented by the Kenya Climate Change Working Group (KCCWG) through working in close collaboration with the Parliamentary Committee on Renewable Energy and Climate Change (PANERECC), and actively engaging the Kenya Populace in climate change issues. The project is closely linked to ongoing CAFOD work on Sustainable Livelihoods and Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation.</narrative>
  </description>
